Thought:[32;1m[1;3mFinal Answer:

Let $I$ be the set of products, indexed by their "Product Name" as given below. For each product $i \in I$, let:

- $r_i$ = Revenue for product $i$ (from "Revenue" column)
- $d_i$ = Demand for product $i$ (from "Demand" column)
- $s_i$ = Initial Inventory for product $i$ (from "Initial Inventory" column)
- $x_i$ = Number of units of product $i$ to fulfill (decision variable, nonnegative integer)

The complete mathematical model is:

$$
\begin{align*}
\text{Maximize} \quad & \sum_{i \in I} r_i x_i \\[2ex]
\text{subject to} \quad
& 0 \leq x_i \leq \min\{d_i,\, s_i\} \qquad \forall i \in I \\
& x_i \in \mathbb{Z}_{\geq 0} \qquad\qquad\qquad\quad\,\,\,\, \forall i \in I
\end{align*}
$$

